# Closer

Two-person long-distance couple space. No chat or video calls.

- Read `docs/spec.md` and `docs/backlog.md` before coding. One backlog task at a time.
- Update `docs/openapi.yaml` before changing an endpoint. It is the source of truth.
- Every task ships tests. Each data endpoint has a cross-couple denial test.
- Scope every query by the caller's `couple_id`. Hash passwords. Use a short-lived JWT. Invite codes are single-use, expiring, and rate-limited.
- Call an LLM only when that couple has opted in. Do not log personal content or prompts.
- Store datetimes in UTC. Convert with the user's IANA timezone in the UI.
- Keep secrets in env vars listed in `.env.example`.
- After a task, tick `docs/backlog.md` and append the prompt to `docs/ai-log.md`.

A visit lookup must include the couple. Filter `Visit.couple_id == couple.id` with the visit id. Do not load a visit by id alone.
